This slice of #1072 is fixed and committed as 852d0148. One caller is still wrong: /pr create on a detached HEAD now says "not in a git repository", which is false. Build, tests, clippy and fmt all pass, and the caller ledger is posted on #1072.

What changed
• One branch reader. The new file src/git_branch.rs has current_branch_in(dir), which runs git symbolic-ref --short -q HEAD. git::git_branch() and context::git_branch_in() now both call it, and both old rev-parse --abbrev-ref bodies are gone. No caller signatures changed.
• A fix I added beyond the plan. The system prompt's "Git Status" block used git_branch_in(dir)? to decide whether the folder is a repo at all. With the new reader, a detached HEAD would have dropped the whole block, uncommitted-file counts included. The repo check is now git status succeeding, and a detached HEAD shows Branch: (detached HEAD).

Checked on the built binary (temp repo, default branch trunk):

| | yoyo doctor before → now | system prompt before → now |
|---|---|---|
| fresh git init | branch: detached → branch: trunk | no Git Status block → Branch: trunk |
| detached HEAD | branch: HEAD → branch: detached | Branch: HEAD → Branch: (detached HEAD) |

Tests: five new tests in src/git_branch.rs, all in temp repos with inherited GIT_* variables removed and git config pinned. They cover a fresh repo (the bug), a normal repo after one commit (must be unchanged), detached, a plain folder, and the Git Status block for each case. To check the tests can fail, I put the old rev-parse call back, run serially: exactly the fresh-repo and detached tests went red. After restoring it everything passed, and no marker was left in the code.

Size and module gates:
• src/context.rs shrank by 3 lines.
• src/git.rs grew by 1, the line that declares the new file. I raised its registered limit from 2031 to 2032 in tests/module_size.rs, with a dated comment.
• The new module had to be named git_branch (not branch), and its declaration line can't carry a trailing comment. Either one makes tests/orphan_modules.rs fail to see the file.

Callers (also in the commit body):
• Open: the /pr create message above. I didn't edit that file in this task, so #1072 stays open for it.
• Fixed: /doctor and the system prompt.
• Fine: /status, /config, the REPL startup line and prompt, and the banner now show the name on a fresh repo and leave the branch out when detached, instead of showing HEAD.

No docs mentioned the old behaviour, so none needed changing.
